From 86e1f7ae08c30d56678c50d56c9d087f66a79ca3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 16:31:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] LAN: separate reply queue; don't stall on clients that
 left

Mirror LocalMP, where Download Play works: replies go to their own
queue read only by RecvReplies(); everything else is delivered in order
by RecvPacket()/RecvHostPacket(). Previously one queue was shared and
each reader destroyed frames of the other kind, so the host never saw a
client's deauthentication (or the downloaded game reconnecting) while
waiting for replies.

After a client misses 3 polls in a row, wait for it only briefly until
it answers again. A Download Play client that rebooted into the
downloaded game cost the host the full wait (300ms) per poll, so the
host reached its multiplayer lobby after the client had stopped
searching ("connection interrupted").

Handshake waits now only follow requests (auth seq 1, (re)assoc, probe),
not responses or deauths, which never get an answer. Clear queues when
a console switches Wi-Fi on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013NwZqgQSwwvXin9eSMf3Cf
